<body>

<table width=100%><tr><td bgcolor=#3A2A1E class=c style="padding:24px">
<p style="margin:0"><span class="go b" style="font-size:11pt">&#127867;&nbsp;&nbsp;THE GAME DIRECTOR'S CONCEPT BRIEF</span></p>
<p style="margin:2px 0 0"><span class=cr style="font-size:33pt;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:1px">HEARTHBOUND HOLLOW</span></p>
<p style="margin:2px 0 8px"><span style="color:#E9CF9F;font-size:13pt;font-style:italic">A Cozy Memory-Broker Narrative Simulation</span></p>
<p style="margin:0"><span style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:12.5pt;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic">&#8220;Some memories want to be sold. Some don't.&#8221;</span></p>
<p style="margin:10px 0 0"><span style="color:#CFBEA6;font-size:9pt">Stardew's warmth &times; Spiritfarer's heart &times; Strange Horticulture's puzzles &times; Disco Elysium's writing &mdash; at cozy scale</span></p>
</td></tr></table>
<p style="margin:4px 0"></p>

<table width=100%><tr>
<td bgcolor=#F4E7CE class=c style="padding:8px"><p style="margin:0"><span class="am b" style="font-size:8.5pt">GENRE</span></p><p style="margin:0;font-size:8.6pt">Cozy life-sim &middot; Narrative investigation &middot; Magical realism</p></td>
<td bgcolor=#EEDCBE class=c style="padding:8px"><p style="margin:0"><span class="am b" style="font-size:8.5pt">MODE</span></p><p style="margin:0;font-size:8.6pt">Single-player &middot; No combat &middot; No fail-state</p></td>
<td bgcolor=#F4E7CE class=c style="padding:8px"><p style="margin:0"><span class="am b" style="font-size:8.5pt">PLATFORM</span></p><p style="margin:0;font-size:8.6pt">PC / Steam + Switch Day-1 &rarr; Mobile &rarr; PS5 / Xbox</p></td>
<td bgcolor=#EEDCBE class=c style="padding:8px"><p style="margin:0"><span class="am b" style="font-size:8.5pt">PRICE &middot; LAUNCH</span></p><p style="margin:0;font-size:8.6pt">$24.99 base &middot; $9.99 mobile &middot; Target 2027</p></td>
</tr></table>
<p style="margin:4px 0"></p>

<table width=100%><tr><td bgcolor=#F7ECCF style="padding:11px 14px;border-left:5px solid #B56A1E">
<span class="am b" style="font-size:9pt">THE PITCH IN ONE BREATH&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span>You inherit <span class=b>The Hollow</span> &mdash; a memory-brokerage shop in a quiet autumn village, abandoned by its mysterious previous keeper. Memories are physical, glowing glass orbs you can <span class="ru b">buy, sell, restore, and find.</span> Every villager carries a hand-authored life story locked in orbs &mdash; and every transaction is a choice with weight. Beneath the warmth lies one question: <span class="pl b i">why did the previous keeper vanish?</span>
</td></tr></table>

<div class=h>01&nbsp;&nbsp;The Concept &amp; The Market Gap</div>
<p>Cozy games oversaturate the <span class="sg b">farming + relationships</span> axis &mdash; every Stardew clone fights for the same audience. The <span class="am b">cozy-narrative-investigation</span> axis is wide open. Spiritfarer proved 2M+ players want emotional weight in cozy; Strange Horticulture proved tactile shop-investigation works. <span class=b>Nobody has fused them into one premium title.</span></p>
<table width=100%><tr>
<td bgcolor=#2B1E16 style="padding:10px 12px;width:44%">
<p style="margin:0 0 3px"><span class="go b" style="font-size:8.5pt">THE OPEN QUADRANT</span></p>
<pre class=mono>        HIGH NARRATIVE DEPTH
                &#9650;
   &#9733; HEARTHBOUND &#9474; &bull; Disco Elysium
      HOLLOW     &#9474; &bull; Spiritfarer
                 &#9474; &bull; Strange Hort.
  COZY &#9668;---------&#9532;---------&#9658; DARK
                 &#9474; &bull; Stardew Valley
                 &#9474; &bull; Animal Crossing
                 &#9660;
        LOW NARRATIVE DEPTH</pre>
</td>
<td bgcolor=#E6EBDB style="padding:10px 12px;width:56%">
<p style="margin:0 0 3px"><span class="sg b" style="font-size:8.5pt">VALIDATED DEMAND SIGNALS</span></p>
<p style="margin:0 0 2px;font-size:9pt;line-height:1.1"><span class="am b">&#9656; </span><span class=b>r/CozyGamers (480k) &mdash; </span>#1 complaint: &#8220;Stardew clones all share one farming loop &mdash; I want story depth.&#8221;</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 2px;font-size:9pt;line-height:1.1"><span class="am b">&#9656; </span><span class=b>Coral Island &mdash; </span>8M+ wishlists &mdash; proves cozy market scale.</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 2px;font-size:9pt;line-height:1.1"><span class="am b">&#9656; </span><span class=b>Spiritfarer &mdash; </span>2M+ sales &mdash; proves audience for &#8220;cozy with weight.&#8221;</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 2px;font-size:9pt;line-height:1.1"><span class="am b">&#9656; </span><span class=b>Strange Horticulture &mdash; </span>500k+ at 96% positive &mdash; validates shop-investigation.</p>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:9pt;line-height:1.1"><span class="am b">&#9656; </span><span class=b>TikTok #CozyGames &mdash; </span>4.8B+ views &mdash; orb-polishing is short-form video gold.</p>
</td></tr></table>
<p class=c style="margin:3px 0;font-size:8.8pt;font-style:italic;color:#6B5D52">Estimated TAM $25&ndash;50M &middot; conservative 3-yr projection ~$44.7M gross / ~$26M net &middot; no gacha, no energy, no P2W &mdash; trust is the moat.</p>

<div class=h style="border-left-color:#5C6E3F">02&nbsp;&nbsp;The Core Loop</div>
<div class=s style="border-left-color:#5C6E3F">One in-game day &asymp; 20&ndash;35 min. Calm, repeatable, hand-authored &mdash; never grindy.</div>
<table width=100%><tr>
<td bgcolor=#F4E7CE class=c style="padding:8px 6px"><p style="margin:0;font-size:17pt">&#127749;</p><p style="margin:1px 0"><span class="am b" style="font-size:8.2pt">1. MORNING</span></p><p style="margin:0;font-size:7.6pt;line-height:1.05">Tend the shop, polish jars, brew tea.</p></td>
<td bgcolor=#F7ECCF class=c style="padding:8px 6px"><p style="margin:0;font-size:17pt">&#128276;</p><p style="margin:1px 0"><span class="am b" style="font-size:8.2pt">2. OPEN SHOP</span></p><p style="margin:0;font-size:7.6pt;line-height:1.05">Villagers visit with one of four needs.</p></td>
<td bgcolor=#F4E7CE class=c style="padding:8px 6px"><p style="margin:0;font-size:17pt">&#128302;</p><p style="margin:1px 0"><span class="am b" style="font-size:8.2pt">3. WORKBENCH</span></p><p style="margin:0;font-size:7.6pt;line-height:1.05">Polish &middot; Cleanse &middot; Weave &middot; Sever orbs.</p></td>
<td bgcolor=#F7ECCF class=c style="padding:8px 6px"><p style="margin:0;font-size:17pt">&#127807;</p><p style="margin:1px 0"><span class="am b" style="font-size:8.2pt">4. VILLAGE WALK</span></p><p style="margin:0;font-size:7.6pt;line-height:1.05">Deliver memories, harvest herbs, talk.</p></td>
<td bgcolor=#F4E7CE class=c style="padding:8px 6px"><p style="margin:0;font-size:17pt">&#128214;</p><p style="margin:1px 0"><span class="am b" style="font-size:8.2pt">5. EVENING LEDGER</span></p><p style="margin:0;font-size:7.6pt;line-height:1.05">Review the day; keep / sell / experience. Saves.</p></td>
<td bgcolor=#EAE0E8 class=c style="padding:8px 6px"><p style="margin:0;font-size:17pt">&#128164;</p><p style="margin:1px 0"><span class="am b" style="font-size:8.2pt">6. MEMORY DREAM</span></p><p style="margin:0;font-size:7.6pt;line-height:1.05">Sleep into an illustrated narrative vignette.</p></td>
</tr></table>
<p class=c style="margin:3px 0"><span class="sg b" style="font-size:8.6pt">&rarr; &rarr; &rarr; &nbsp; the cycle loops, and the village quietly changes around your choices &nbsp; &#8635;</span></p>
<table width=100% border=1 style="border:1px solid #E5D3B3"><tr>
<td bgcolor=#FBF3E4 class=c style="padding:7px 9px"><p style="margin:0"><span style="font-size:12pt">&#128148;</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="ru b" style="font-size:9.5pt">TO SELL</span></p><p style="margin:0;font-size:8.2pt;line-height:1.05">a painful memory they want to be rid of</p></td>
<td bgcolor=#FBF3E4 class=c style="padding:7px 9px"><p style="margin:0"><span style="font-size:12pt">&#10024;</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="ru b" style="font-size:9.5pt">TO BUY</span></p><p style="margin:0;font-size:8.2pt;line-height:1.05">a memory they yearn for but never lived</p></td>
<td bgcolor=#FBF3E4 class=c style="padding:7px 9px"><p style="margin:0"><span style="font-size:12pt">&#128302;</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="ru b" style="font-size:9.5pt">TO RESTORE</span></p><p style="margin:0;font-size:8.2pt;line-height:1.05">a memory that has faded and cracked</p></td>
<td bgcolor=#FBF3E4 class=c style="padding:7px 9px"><p style="margin:0"><span style="font-size:12pt">&#128269;</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="ru b" style="font-size:9.5pt">TO FIND</span></p><p style="margin:0;font-size:8.2pt;line-height:1.05">a memory someone else lost or stole</p></td>
</tr></table>
<p class=c style="margin:1px 0;font-size:8.4pt;font-style:italic;color:#6B5D52">Every visitor arrives with one of these four needs &mdash; the engine of every day.</p>

<div class=h>03&nbsp;&nbsp;The Pillar Mechanics</div>
<div class=s>Five interlocking systems. Tactile over textual &mdash; if a feeling can be felt through an orb, prefer it over text.</div>

<table width=100%><tr><td bgcolor=#F7ECCF style="padding:11px 14px;border-left:4px solid #B56A1E">
<p style="margin:0 0 3px"><span class="b" style="color:#B56A1E;font-size:12pt">A&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span class=b style="font-size:12pt">Memory Orbs &mdash; the tactile core</span></p>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:9.6pt">Memories take physical form as glass orbs you physically drag, sort, polish, and weave on your shelves. Four readable properties tell you everything before a single word of dialogue:</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 0 10px;font-size:9.3pt;line-height:1.1"><span class="am b">&bull; </span><span class=b>Colour </span>= emotional tone (joy, grief, shame, awe, longing, dread&hellip;)</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 0 10px;font-size:9.3pt;line-height:1.1"><span class="am b">&bull; </span><span class=b>Clarity </span>= how intact the memory is</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 0 10px;font-size:9.3pt;line-height:1.1"><span class="am b">&bull; </span><span class=b>Cracks </span>= trauma &mdash; cleanse carelessly and you erase the truth</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 0 10px;font-size:9.3pt;line-height:1.1"><span class="am b">&bull; </span><span class=b>Weight </span>= significance to the person who gave it</p>
</td></tr></table><p style="margin:4px 0"></p>

<table width=100%><tr><td bgcolor=#F3E2DA style="padding:11px 14px;border-left:4px solid #9C3E1A">
<p style="margin:0 0 3px"><span class="b" style="color:#9C3E1A;font-size:12pt">B&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span class=b style="font-size:12pt">The Workbench &mdash; the crafting core</span></p>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:9.6pt">Four operations, each a short (&lt;90s) tactile mini-game with an always-visible <span class="ru b i">&#8220;do it for me&#8221;</span> auto-complete. Every villager has unique tolerances &mdash; some want grief cleansed; others would never forgive you for taking it.</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 0 10px;font-size:9.3pt;line-height:1.1"><span class="ru b">&bull; </span><span class=b>Polish </span>&mdash; restore clarity to a faded orb (slow circular motion)</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 0 10px;font-size:9.3pt;line-height:1.1"><span class="ru b">&bull; </span><span class=b>Cleanse </span>&mdash; remove cracks/trauma (pattern trace) &middot; risk: erase too much</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 0 10px;font-size:9.3pt;line-height:1.1"><span class="ru b">&bull; </span><span class=b>Weave </span>&mdash; combine two memories into one stronger memory (tessellation)</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 0 10px;font-size:9.3pt;line-height:1.1"><span class="ru b">&bull; </span><span class=b>Sever </span>&mdash; split a complex memory into its components (reverse tessellation)</p>
</td></tr></table><p style="margin:4px 0"></p>

<table width=100%><tr><td bgcolor=#EAE0E8 style="padding:11px 14px;border-left:4px solid #5B3955">
<p style="margin:0 0 3px"><span class="b" style="color:#5B3955;font-size:12pt">C&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span class=b style="font-size:12pt">The Echo Web &amp; Village Ledger &mdash; the narrative core</span></p>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:9.6pt">Every villager hides a <span class="pl b">Memory Map</span> &mdash; 12&ndash;20 memories that reconstruct their whole life. Orbs carry hidden <span class="pl b">Echoes</span> (shared faces, places, objects, years); collecting linked memories lights a thread between them in your Codex and unlocks <span class="pl b">Revelation chapters.</span> Doris's wedding-day crowd hides a face from the Mayor's first regret &mdash; and the whole village is one woven thing.</p>
</td></tr></table><p style="margin:4px 0"></p>

<table width=100%><tr><td bgcolor=#F7ECCF style="padding:11px 14px;border-left:4px solid #8A4B12">
<p style="margin:0 0 3px"><span class="b" style="color:#8A4B12;font-size:12pt">D&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span class=b style="font-size:12pt">The Moral Compass &mdash; the 7 Vows / the choice core</span></p>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:9.6pt">Unlike farming sims, <span class="am b">every transaction is a choice.</span> A widower asks you to erase his late wife &mdash; do you? A lonely child wants to buy a stranger's father-memory. The Keeper lives by <span class="am b">seven Vows</span> (Consent &middot; Return &middot; Whole &middot; Quiet Glass &middot; Honest Coin &middot; Open Door &middot; Last Light). Vows aren't a morality bar &mdash; they quietly shape how every villager responds to you over seasons.</p>
</td></tr></table><p style="margin:4px 0"></p>

<table width=100%><tr><td bgcolor=#E6EBDB style="padding:11px 14px;border-left:4px solid #5C6E3F">
<p style="margin:0 0 3px"><span class="b" style="color:#5C6E3F;font-size:12pt">E&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span class=b style="font-size:12pt">Memory Tea &amp; The Garden &mdash; the cozy anchor</span></p>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:9.6pt">A small herb garden behind the Hollow (lavender, valerian, sage, mugwort&hellip;). Brew teas that help villagers <span class="sg b">open up &mdash; or temporarily forget.</span> This is the comfort/idle loop that lets the game breathe between heavy moments.</p>
</td></tr></table>

<div class=h style="border-left-color:#5B3955">04&nbsp;&nbsp;Progression &mdash; How The Game Grows</div>
<div class=s style="border-left-color:#5B3955">Replayable on emotion, not grind. New playthroughs explore different residents, not new mechanics.</div>
<p>Progress is woven from people, not XP bars. The game silently tracks a <span class="pl b">14-dimension Village State</span> (per-villager Trust, Memory Integrity, the 7 Vow integrities, Pickle's approval, Coin &amp; Cinder, Hollow level, Echo connections, the predecessor trail&hellip;). <span class="gy i">You never see a number &mdash; you infer the consequence.</span></p>
<table width=100%><tr>
<td bgcolor=#FBF3E4 style="padding:10px 12px;width:50%">
<p style="margin:0 0 3px"><span class="am b" style="font-size:9pt">WHAT DEEPENS AS YOU PLAY</span></p>
<p style="margin:0 0 1px;font-size:9.2pt;line-height:1.1"><span class="go b">&#10022; </span>Villager Trust &amp; their Memory Maps fill in</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 1px;font-size:9.2pt;line-height:1.1"><span class="go b">&#10022; </span>Vow integrities shift, re-shaping the village</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 1px;font-size:9.2pt;line-height:1.1"><span class="go b">&#10022; </span>The Echo Web threads more memories together</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 1px;font-size:9.2pt;line-height:1.1"><span class="go b">&#10022; </span>Hollow upgrades + a 2nd progression track (Garden)</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 1px;font-size:9.2pt;line-height:1.1"><span class="go b">&#10022; </span>The Coin &amp; Cinder economy (Cinder = Listen-path only)</p>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:9.2pt;line-height:1.1"><span class="go b">&#10022; </span>The grand mystery of the predecessor, Marin</p>
</td>
<td bgcolor=#EAE0E8 style="padding:10px 12px;width:50%">
<p style="margin:0 0 3px"><span class="pl b" style="font-size:9pt">MISSION ARC (THE LONG ROAD)</span></p>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:9.2pt;line-height:1.05"><span class="pl b">&#9656; </span><span class=b>M1 &middot; Opening the Hollow</span><span style="font-size:8.6pt"> &mdash; meet Doris &middot; polish your first orb</span></p>
<p style="margin:0 0 2px 12px"><span class="gy i" style="font-size:8pt">&#9989; playable</span></p>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:9.2pt;line-height:1.05"><span class="pl b">&#9656; </span><span class=b>M2 &middot; The Widower's Request</span><span style="font-size:8.6pt"> &mdash; Gerrold &middot; the first moral choice</span></p>
<p style="margin:0 0 2px 12px"><span class="gy i" style="font-size:8pt">&#9989; playable</span></p>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:9.2pt;line-height:1.05"><span class="pl b">&#9656; </span><span class=b>M3&ndash;M10</span><span style="font-size:8.6pt"> &mdash; 30+ villagers &middot; Weave/Sever &middot; seasons</span></p>
<p style="margin:0 0 2px 12px"><span class="gy i" style="font-size:8pt">&#9635; post-greenlight</span></p>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:9.2pt;line-height:1.05"><span class="pl b">&#9656; </span><span class=b>Full game</span><span style="font-size:8.6pt"> &mdash; the predecessor revealed &middot; ~45&ndash;60 hrs</span></p>
<p style="margin:0 0 0 12px"><span class="gy i" style="font-size:8pt">&#9635; scaling ref</span></p>
</td></tr></table>
<p style="margin:3px 0"></p>
<table width=100%><tr><td bgcolor=#F7ECCF style="padding:11px 14px;border-left:5px solid #5C6E3F">
<span class="am b" style="font-size:9pt">THE VERTICAL SLICE TODAY&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span>A fully playable, polished <span class=b>Mission 1 + Mission 2</span> in Unity 6 &mdash; six scenes, two villager arcs, four moral choices, two Memory Dreams, full comfort/accessibility layer. ~55&ndash;75 minutes of cozy. Build v0.5.0. Next gate: a 20-person greenlight playtest (target: 14/20 say &#8220;I want to play more&#8221;).
</td></tr></table>

<div class=h>05&nbsp;&nbsp;How To Play &mdash; A Guide For The Director</div>
<div class=s>The complete mechanical vocabulary of the playable slice. No HUD. No combat. Tension is moral, not mechanical.</div>
<p style="margin:0 0 4px"><span class="am b" style="font-size:9.5pt">THE CORE VERBS &mdash; everything you actually do</span></p>
<table width=100% border=1 style="border:1px solid #E5D3B3">
<tr><td bgcolor=#F7ECCF style="padding:5px 9px;width:26%"><span class=b style="font-size:9.6pt">&#128694; Walk</span></td><td bgcolor=#F7ECCF style="padding:5px 9px;font-size:9.2pt">Camera-relative WASD / stick. Slow autumn pace. Sprint + Jump (off in Gentle Mode).</td></tr>
<tr><td bgcolor=#FBF3E4 style="padding:5px 9px"><span class=b style="font-size:9.6pt">&#128066; Listen</span></td><td bgcolor=#FBF3E4 style="padding:5px 9px;font-size:9.2pt">Watch the speaker; pick 1 of 2&ndash;6 options that almost always include &#8220;(silent nod).&#8221; You never have to speak first.</td></tr>
<tr><td bgcolor=#F7ECCF style="padding:5px 9px"><span class=b style="font-size:9.6pt">&#128270; Examine</span></td><td bgcolor=#F7ECCF style="padding:5px 9px;font-size:9.2pt">Press E near any glowing prop to read its codex tooltip. Many props seed the long-arc story.</td></tr>
<tr><td bgcolor=#FBF3E4 style="padding:5px 9px"><span class=b style="font-size:9.6pt">&#10024; Polish</span></td><td bgcolor=#FBF3E4 style="padding:5px 9px;font-size:9.2pt">Hold to draw slow circles over a faded orb; the memory clears as you work (~70&ndash;90s).</td></tr>
<tr><td bgcolor=#F7ECCF style="padding:5px 9px"><span class=b style="font-size:9.6pt">&#127861; Brew</span></td><td bgcolor=#F7ECCF style="padding:5px 9px;font-size:9.2pt">Harvest a herb &rarr; steep at the kettle &rarr; pour &rarr; carry the cup. ~12 real seconds of warmth.</td></tr>
<tr><td bgcolor=#FBF3E4 style="padding:5px 9px"><span class=b style="font-size:9.6pt">&#129657; Cleanse</span></td><td bgcolor=#FBF3E4 style="padding:5px 9px;font-size:9.2pt">Trace each crack without crossing the warm core (~70&ndash;100s). Real consequences, never a &#8220;FAILED&#8221; screen.</td></tr>
<tr><td bgcolor=#F7ECCF style="padding:5px 9px"><span class=b style="font-size:9.6pt">&#9878; Choose</span></td><td bgcolor=#F7ECCF style="padding:5px 9px;font-size:9.2pt">Read four sentences in fiction-voice; press a button. The heaviest choice asks you to confirm twice.</td></tr>
<tr><td bgcolor=#FBF3E4 style="padding:5px 9px"><span class=b style="font-size:9.6pt">&#128213; Sleep / Close the Ledger</span></td><td bgcolor=#FBF3E4 style="padding:5px 9px;font-size:9.2pt">Close a leather-bound book at day's end &mdash; that is the only save. A dream plays. Morning comes.</td></tr>
</table>
<p style="margin:4px 0"></p>
<table width=100%><tr>
<td bgcolor=#2B1E16 style="padding:10px 13px;width:42%">
<p style="margin:0 0 3px"><span class="go b" style="font-size:9.5pt">&#9000;&nbsp;&nbsp;KEY CONTROLS</span></p>
<p style="margin:0 0 1px;font-size:8.8pt"><span class=cr>Move&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span class="go b">WASD / Stick</span></p>
<p style="margin:0 0 1px;font-size:8.8pt"><span class=cr>Interact / Examine&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span class="go b">E / &#9643;</span></p>
<p style="margin:0 0 1px;font-size:8.8pt"><span class=cr>Polish &middot; Cleanse&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span class="go b">Hold LMB + draw</span></p>
<p style="margin:0 0 1px;font-size:8.8pt"><span class=cr>Camera look / zoom&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span class="go b">RMB drag / scroll</span></p>
<p style="margin:0 0 1px;font-size:8.8pt"><span class=cr>Open Codex (Memory Map)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span class="go b">C</span></p>
<p style="margin:0 0 1px;font-size:8.8pt"><span class=cr>Help card / Pause&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span class="go b">H / Esc</span></p>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:8.8pt"><span class=cr>Skip cutscene&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span class="go b">Hold Space 0.8s</span></p>
</td>
<td bgcolor=#E6EBDB style="padding:10px 13px;width:58%">
<p style="margin:0 0 3px"><span class="sg b" style="font-size:9.5pt">&#128367;&nbsp;&nbsp;THE COZY CONTRACT &mdash; six promises</span></p>
<p style="margin:0 0 1px;font-size:9pt;line-height:1.1"><span class="sg b">1. </span>Nothing punishes kindness.</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 1px;font-size:9pt;line-height:1.1"><span class="sg b">2. </span>Failure is narratively absorbed, never scored.</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 1px;font-size:9pt;line-height:1.1"><span class="sg b">3. </span>No time pressure unless you ask for it.</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 1px;font-size:9pt;line-height:1.1"><span class="sg b">4. </span>Refusal is always honoured &mdash; sometimes it's the best path.</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 1px;font-size:9pt;line-height:1.1"><span class="sg b">5. </span>No content surprises (the Tone Compass warns you first).</p>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:9pt;line-height:1.1"><span class="sg b">6. </span>Auto-Complete is always available for every mini-game.</p>
</td></tr></table>
<p style="margin:4px 0"></p>
<table width=100%><tr><td bgcolor=#EAE0E8 style="padding:10px 14px;border-left:4px solid #5B3955">
<span class=b style="font-size:9.5pt">&#128008;&nbsp;&nbsp;MEET PICKLE&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span>A slate-grey, sarcastic, telepathic cat &mdash; the only living thing the previous Keeper left behind. She judges every decision, but you only earn her commentary by being kind. <span class=b>Plus:</span> Gentle Mode, Auto-Complete, colour-blind &amp; dyslexia options, per-character voice sliders, and Heavy-Theme warning cards &mdash; comfort is first-class, and nothing ever locks you out of content.
</td></tr></table>

<div class=h style="border-left-color:#9C3E1A">06&nbsp;&nbsp;Why It Wins &mdash; USPs &amp; Director's Takeaways</div>
<table width=100% border=1 style="border:1px solid #E5D3B3">
<tr>
<td bgcolor=#FBF3E4 class=c style="padding:9px 11px;width:33%"><p style="margin:0;font-size:15pt">&#128302;</p><p style="margin:1px 0"><span class="ru b" style="font-size:9.2pt">A novel core mechanic</span></p><p style="margin:0;font-size:8.3pt;line-height:1.1">Memories as a physical, tradable commodity &mdash; never attempted at this depth. Tactile, dramatic, replayable, and engineered for short-form video.</p></td>
<td bgcolor=#F7ECCF class=c style="padding:9px 11px;width:33%"><p style="margin:0;font-size:15pt">&#128151;</p><p style="margin:1px 0"><span class="ru b" style="font-size:9.2pt">Cozy with real weight</span></p><p style="margin:0;font-size:8.3pt;line-height:1.1">Every transaction has lasting village consequences. The cozy crowd that cried at Spiritfarer is waiting for this.</p></td>
<td bgcolor=#FBF3E4 class=c style="padding:9px 11px;width:34%"><p style="margin:0;font-size:15pt">&#128214;</p><p style="margin:1px 0"><span class="ru b" style="font-size:9.2pt">Every villager is a mystery</span></p><p style="margin:0;font-size:8.3pt;line-height:1.1">30+ residents, each a hand-authored, fully reconstructable memory map &mdash; depth without farming grind.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td bgcolor=#F7ECCF class=c style="padding:9px 11px"><p style="margin:0;font-size:15pt">&#127902;</p><p style="margin:1px 0"><span class="ru b" style="font-size:9.2pt">Memory Dreams</span></p><p style="margin:0;font-size:8.3pt;line-height:1.1">Every collected memory becomes a branching illustrated vignette &mdash; perpetual, low-cost narrative content.</p></td>
<td bgcolor=#FBF3E4 class=c style="padding:9px 11px"><p style="margin:0;font-size:15pt">&#128367;</p><p style="margin:1px 0"><span class="ru b" style="font-size:9.2pt">No combat. No death. No grind.</span></p><p style="margin:0;font-size:8.3pt;line-height:1.1">Clean positioning against farming-sim fatigue; tension is purely moral.</p></td>
<td bgcolor=#F7ECCF class=c style="padding:9px 11px"><p style="margin:0;font-size:15pt">&#129526;</p><p style="margin:1px 0"><span class="ru b" style="font-size:9.2pt">A grand mystery underneath</span></p><p style="margin:0;font-size:8.3pt;line-height:1.1">Who was the previous Keeper, and why did they leave? The thread that pulls players to the end.</p></td>
</tr>
</table>
<p style="margin:6px 0"></p>
<table width=100%><tr><td bgcolor=#3A2A1E class=c style="padding:14px 18px">
<p style="margin:0"><span class=cr style="font-size:11pt;font-style:italic">&#8220;The shop should feel like a real place. The villagers should feel like real people.</span></p>
<p style="margin:0"><span class=cr style="font-size:11pt;font-style:italic">The choices should hurt a little. And the soundtrack should make people cry on the bus.&#8221;</span></p>
<p style="margin:4px 0 0"><span class="go b" style="font-size:8.5pt">&mdash; The Hearthbound Hollow vision</span></p>
</td></tr></table>
